                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Okayyyy, so this is the most popular poker game, other than VR poker games. I will say though, while it is fun for a minute, there are so many exploits that I am seeing, or the people that are usually playing at all times could possibly be cheating somehow. Yes, I am fine losing a hand 3 or 4 times, but when someone and another person in the same game, are punting their stacks at each other equally. The one I know is exploiting, or cheating, was getting flush hands every hand for about 20 minutes. Like, Bro would win, the next hand, he would donate half of his stack to (i guess) his homie. There has never been a person that has even been close to that. In real poker as well as casino's on the internet. To get a flush that many times in a row, one is sus. Two, he would donate to a specific person on the table after winning. So i would say that when you get this game, think of it already, as the house wins. Only it is not a casino, but one or maybe more people. Straight-up. Oh also this is not me saying it for no reason there are community feeds about it and also it is known in the community, either figure out the exploits or (in my case) you can sometimes win even though they either know what the flop, turn, and river are or they fold.  Another example would be the fact that you will see a flop coming all Kings, or queens, or whatever. It will all come but never for you. So just be aware of the, I would say toxic ass community. I was also sub-100 of the leaderboard of chips gained. SO yes, you can win some games, but honestly more times i had to leave that table more times than playing a single table. Facking annoying",
